        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: Loksatta\n- People: Ravi Amale, Malik Amber\n- Places: Mumbai, Pune, Nagpur, Ahmednagar, Aurangabad, Delhi, Aurangabad Division, Marathwada region\n- Roles: senior editor\n- Topics: newspaper publishing, city founding, administrative headquarters, city nicknames\n\nFacts:\n- Aurangabad was founded in 1610 by Malik Amber.\n- In 2010, Aurangabad completed 400 years since its founding.\n- Aurangabad is the administrative headquarters of the Aurangabad Division or Marathwada region.\n- Aurangabad is titled \"The City of Gates.\"\n- Loksatta is published out of Mumbai, Pune, Nagpur, Ahmednagar, Aurangabad, and Delhi.\n- Ravi Amale is the senior editor of Loksatta.\n- Loksatta is a leading Marathi daily in Mumbai.",
